  "When a user needs more precise visual context, the OpenStreetMap tab loads standard raster tiles for the visible area after explicit consent. This view normally shows much more local detail than the bundled SVG tiles, but it sends the user's IP address, request headers, referrer, and requested tile coordinates to OpenStreetMap. Its database is licensed under ODbL, and hosted tiles follow separate usage requirements.": "当用户需要更精确的视觉参考时，OpenStreetMap 标签页会在获得明确同意后加载可见区域的标准栅格图块。该视图通常比随应用提供的 SVG 图块显示更多本地细节，但会把用户的 IP 地址、请求标头、来源页面以及所请求图块的坐标发送给 OpenStreetMap。其数据库采用 ODbL 许可，托管图块还须遵守单独的使用要求。"
